<Project>
  <!--
  This repo is checked out directly inside the live BepInEx/plugins folder (a deliberate choice
  for a fast dev loop: edit here, build here, restart the game). The problem is that BepInEx
  recursively scans every .dll under BepInEx/plugins, so leaving bin/obj at their default
  location meant every build — Debug or Release, main project or Tests — silently produced a
  second, independently loadable copy of the plugin sitting right next to whatever was properly
  deployed. Multiple copies then race for BepInEx's "load the newer one" logic, which is exactly
  how a stale build ended up running instead of a fresh one (see the plugin-version fix in
  LegacyHelper.Core.cs for the other half of that bug).

  Redirecting bin/obj out from under BepInEx/plugins entirely removes the possibility of that
  happening again, structurally, rather than by convention or by remembering to clean up after
  every build. Both projects import this file automatically (standard MSBuild SDK behaviour),
  so this applies to the Tests project too — its own output previously carried a copy of the
  main plugin DLL as a project-reference artifact, which was just as loadable as any other copy.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <BaseOutputPath>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\..\..\LegacyoftheAbyss-DevBuild\bin\$(MSBuildProjectName)\</BaseOutputPath>
    <BaseIntermediateOutputPath>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\..\..\LegacyoftheAbyss-DevBuild\obj\$(MSBuildProjectName)\</BaseIntermediateOutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
